<BlogPost slug="vivitrol-shot-how-it-works-and-how-long-it-lasts" toc={toc}>
  <p>Vivitrol, also known as naltrexone, is a prescription medicine that helps treat alcohol dependence. It comes as an extended-release injection, meaning the medicine is slowly released in the body over a long period of time.</p>
  <p>Alcohol use disorder (AUD) is one of the most common types of addiction in the U.S., and about 2.1 million people with AUD received treatment in 2024 [1]. Care is effective, and it&rsquo;s possible to fully heal from AUD, but the recovery journey can be uncomfortable and challenging. Vivitrol is a medicine that helps lower cravings for alcohol, improving a person&rsquo;s chances of staying sober, finishing treatment, and making long-term change.</p>

  <h2 id="what-is-the-shot">What Is the Vivitrol Shot?</h2>
  <p>Vivitrol is the brand name for naltrexone, an opioid antagonist. It&rsquo;s used in treatment for alcohol and opioid dependency to prevent the feeling of a euphoric high and reduce cravings. For these uses, it&rsquo;s approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA).</p>
  <p>Vivitrol is a prescription medicine and is only available from, and administered by, a licensed physician. It&rsquo;s given through an intramuscular injection once a month. Once Vivitrol is in the body, it can&rsquo;t be removed.</p>
  <p>Vivitrol is a type of <a href="/programs/medication-assisted-treatment/">medication-assisted treatment (MAT)</a> for addiction, and research shows it helps decrease heavy drinking among people with alcohol dependence [2]. It&rsquo;s not a standalone treatment for alcohol or opioid addiction, though&mdash;Vivitrol works as part of a broader treatment plan that includes psychotherapy and wellness activities.</p>

